                     <summary/>
                     <msItem xml:id="p2_i1">
                        <locus target="#178"/>
                        <title type="incomplete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1932Mashaf">Fragment of a lectionary for the readings
                           during the Holy Week</title>
                        <note>A fragment of an old lectionary, containing the directives as to what
                           should be read during the Holy Week. It enumerates the Biblical books in
                           the form very close to that normally attested in the <ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT2675AC81">Apostolic canons (81)</ref>. Yet, the fragment shows the archaic attribution of
                           this form to the 318 fathers of Nicaea: this attribution is found also in
                           the <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESum039">Bǝḥerāwi Kǝllǝlāwi Mangǝśti Tǝgrāy, ʿUrā Qirqos, UM-039</ref>.
                           <q xml:lang="gez">ግብረ፡ ዓለም፡ ፩።16 ፀአተ፡ ግብጽ፡
                              ፩።17 ሌዋዊያን፡ ፩።18 ኍልቍ፡19 ፩።20 ዳግም፡ ሕግ፡21 ፩።22 ኢያሱ፡23 ዘኔዌ፡24 ፩።25
                              ፈታሕት፡26 ፩።27 ሩት፡28 ፩።29 ነገሥት፡30 ፬።31 ሕጹጻን፡ ፪።32 ዕዝራ፡ ፫።33 መጽሐፈ፡34
                              መዝሙር፡ ፻፶።35 ምሳሌ፡36 ሰሎሞን፡ ፩።37 መክብብ፡ ፩።38 መሓልየ፡ መሓልይ፡ ፩።39 ኢዮብ፡40 ፩።41
                              ነቢያት፡ ንኡሳን፡ ፲፪።42 ኢሳይያስ፡43 ነቢይ፡ ፩።44 ኤርሚያስ፡45 ነቢይ፡ ፩።46 ሕዝቅኤል፡47 ነቢይ፡
